This image, corresponding to Figure 11 from the PDF, visually demonstrates that Nano-11 induces significantly less residual inflammation at the injection site two weeks after injection compared to aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant. The left panel, representing AH, shows extensive granulomatous inflammation with dense cellular aggregates, while the right panel, showing Nano-11, exhibits much milder inflammation characterized by relatively few macrophages arranged in slender cords between muscle fibers, indicating a more transient and resolved local reaction.